Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Bring the five screens to the prototype's anatomy and
 density
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Applies design-prototypes/APPLYING-TO-PRODUCT.md. No frozen document is
touched, no gate is weakened, and no new token is minted.

Content pass first, per § 1. The five screens already satisfied the § 2
mapping: the divergences README.md lists — vanity metrics, delta chips, the
greeting hero, Processing/Failed, on-chain vocabulary, nav outside § 12 — are
in the prototype, not in the product. Verified rather than rewritten.

What crosses, as anatomy and density:

  - Table density. Cells were 6px 8px / 8px; they are now 8px 16px / 12px 16px.
    The prototype pads 13px vertical and 18px horizontal with 11.5px labels,
    and none of those three is on a frozen scale — space runs 12/16/20 and the
    type scale stops at 12. § 5.1 says express the look with existing tokens,
    so this is the nearest rhythm the scales can state. What crosses is the
    shape of the rhythm: tight rows with generous horizontal air.

  - A hairline-framed panel around each table, with the count on the right of
    its head. The prototype draws the same surface with layered shadows and a
    16px radius; § 1.3 puts depth in typography and spacing, and 16px is not on
    the radius scale, so one 1px hairline does the structural work.

  - The filter toolbar: filters left, primary action right. On the beneficiary
    list the action moves out of the page header to get there — the thing you
    do to the list belongs with the controls that shape it.

  - The detail drawer. Drawer was already in the § 5 catalogue, so this is
    composition, not a new primitive. Audited with axe inside the dialog, where
    heading order and labelling most often go wrong.

What deliberately does not cross: the cool ground #EFF4F8, the mint #2FD9A8,
blue Processing, --shadow-card and --shadow-lift, the 16px radius, and the
#93A1B2 micro-labels — the last at roughly 2.6:1, fine as marketing decoration
and a § 7 failure as product content. No glass, ribbons, dotted map or city
silhouette. README.md's "what to take" line names glass; APPLYING-TO-PRODUCT
§ 3 excludes it and § 5.2 makes it a founder decision, and the normative
document wins.

The Alex test stays NOT RUN. § 6 of the applying document is explicit that a
run before the restyle is invalidated by it, so it comes next — with a real
person, and after the Stage 10.5 shell gives them somewhere to click.

Verification: pnpm run verify clean — 83 files, 1654 tests.

