+/*
+ * Density comes from the console prototype, expressed on the frozen scales.
+ *
+ * The prototype pads cells 13px vertical and 18px horizontal and sets its
+ * micro-labels at 11.5px. None of those three is on a scale: space runs
+ * 12 -> 16 -> 20, and the type scale stops at 12. APPLYING-TO-PRODUCT 5.1 is
+ * explicit that the look is expressed with existing tokens rather than by
+ * minting new ones, so this is the nearest rhythm the scales can say:
+ * 12px vertical, 16px horizontal, labels at 12px.
+ *
+ * What actually crosses is the *shape* of that rhythm -- tight rows with
+ * generous horizontal air -- not the exact pixels. 16px also matches the card
